& [StableRustFinding] is safe but incomplete
  + [available] is read_dir, symlink_metadata, MetadataExt.file_attributes, File open, streaming read, and hashing
  + [file_attributes] has been stable since Rust 1.1.0
  + [volume_serial_number] is nightly-only under windows_by_handle issue 63010
  + [number_of_links] is nightly-only under windows_by_handle issue 63010
  + [file_index] is nightly-only under windows_by_handle issue 63010
  + [alternate_stream_enumeration] is absent from stable std
  + [conclusion] is stable std alone cannot prove hard-link or alternate-stream policy

& [ReparseFinding] is reject before descent
  + [attribute] FILE_ATTRIBUTE_REPARSE_POINT is 0x00000400 and covers files or directories with an associated reparse point including symbolic links
  + [open] CreateFileW with FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT prevents normal reparse processing for the terminal entry
  + [directory] FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS is required to obtain a directory handle
  + [profile_0_1] rejects every reparse point regardless of tag
  + [tag] may be captured for diagnosis through FileAttributeTagInfo but is not an admission discriminator
  = must: inspect the entry itself before any descent
  - never: canonicalize or open normally and then claim the alias was not followed

& [IdentityFinding] requires the 128-bit form
  + [legacy_identity] BY_HANDLE_FILE_INFORMATION exposes volume serial, 64-bit file index, and link count
  + [legacy_limit] Microsoft states the 64-bit identifier is not guaranteed unique on ReFS
  + [strong_identity] GetFileInformationByHandleEx with FileIdInfo returns FILE_ID_INFO
  + [identity_tuple] is 64-bit volume serial plus 128-bit file identifier
  + [scope] uniquely identifies a file on one computer according to the API contract
  + [link_count] still comes from BY_HANDLE_FILE_INFORMATION.nNumberOfLinks
  + [lifetime_limit] file identifiers can be reused or can change under filesystem-specific operations
  = must: bind identity observations to one bounded scan and never treat them as timeless object names

& [HardLinkFinding] is fail closed
  + [ordinary_regular_file] requires number_of_links equal to one in profile 0.1
  + [duplicate_identity] rejects two admitted paths with the same strong identity
  + [unsupported_filesystem] rejects absent, partial, or inconsistent identity evidence
  + [outside_alias_limit] link count greater than one proves another name exists but does not enumerate or locate it
  + [policy_effect] rejection does not need to discover the outside alias

& [StreamFinding] is complete named-data-stream accounting
  + [enumeration] FindFirstStreamW yields the first ::$DATA stream and FindNextStreamW continues
  + [file_default] ordinary files have the unnamed ::$DATA stream
  + [directory_default] directories do not have an unnamed data stream by default
  + [profile_0_1] rejects every named ::$DATA stream
  + [unsupported] ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER means the filesystem does not support streams and must be represented explicitly
  + [empty] ERROR_HANDLE_EOF is a distinct no-stream result, not a generic success or failure
  = must: close every stream-enumeration handle with FindClose

& [ProposedAdapter] is one Windows-only observation seam
  + [module] is windows_topology
  + [open_entry_no_follow] returns an owned no-follow handle without exposing a raw handle to callers
  + [query_attributes_and_tag] returns closed attribute and optional diagnostic-tag values
  + [query_strong_identity] returns volume serial and 128-bit file identifier
  + [query_link_count] returns the exact link count or a typed unsupported/error result
  + [enumerate_data_streams] returns bounded canonical stream facts or a typed unsupported/error result
  + [close] is RAII for file and enumeration handles
  + [unsafe] if later authorized is confined to this module and individually justified around generated Win32 calls
  - never: write, delete, rename, create, truncate, follow a reparse point, expose a raw handle, or suppress an operating-system error

& [DependencyDecision] prefers generated bindings
  + [current_lockfile] contains no windows-sys package
  + [candidate] is a direct target-specific windows-sys dependency with only required Win32 feature groups
  + [reason] is generated signatures, structures, constants, and handle types reduce handwritten ABI risk
  + [rejection] is handwritten extern declarations unless a later measured dependency review proves generated bindings unsuitable
  + [authority] is dependency proposal only

& [RaceBoundary] remains visible
  + [handle_strength] querying an opened no-follow handle reduces terminal-path substitution between metadata calls
  + [walk_limit] directory enumeration and opening each child is not an atomic directory snapshot
  + [double_inventory] detects many intervening changes but cannot prove atomicity
  + [candidate_state] must remain quiescent and any identity or inventory drift quarantines the run
  + [seal_strength] remains quiescent_double_inventory unless a separately proven OS snapshot is used
  - never: label double inventory as an atomic snapshot

& [ErrorPolicy] is closed and typed
  + [not_found] is drift
  + [access_denied] is unproven topology
  + [unsupported] is unsupported topology
  + [invalid_encoding] is unrepresentable path
  + [resource_limit] is bounded-scan refusal
  + [changed_during_scan] is quarantine
  + [other_os_error] preserves operation and numeric Windows error without admitting the candidate
  - never: downgrade observation failure to absence

& [ActivationDecision] is form before effect
  + [M2A] is strict scanner request, observation, policy, result, and fault forms with no I/O
  + [M2B] is dependency and unsafe seam review
  + [M2C] is read-only adapter and synthetic fixture implementation only after new authority
  + [M2D] is adversarial fixture execution only after exact fixture-root authorization
  + [current_authority] is M2A specification formation only
